-- title:
--   All places of ℚ̄· F_M have degree one
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive integer. Write $F_M$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb Q((X))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the set `divisorExpansions M`, and let `modularFunctionFieldBar M` be its base change `laurentBaseChange`, namely the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((X))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the image of $F_M$ under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb Q((X)) \to \overline{\mathbb Q}((X))$. The assertion is that every place $w$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has degree one. Here a place consists of a valuation subring of the field `modularFunctionFieldBar M` which contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring; its degree is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-dimension of the residue field of that local ring. Thus the conclusion says that the residue field at every such place is $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ itself, i.e. all places of the base-changed modular function field are rational over the constant field.
--
--   This is the standard fact that over an algebraically closed constant field every place of a function field has residue degree one, here for the function field of the modular curve of level $M$ after base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. It supplies the degree-one hypothesis used throughout the divisor-level Eichler–Shimura bookkeeping and the comparison of places of the characteristic-zero model with those of its reductions.
